1
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa River,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kick a pebble and my shoes go flying too.

3
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:32,960
Onto the head of the carpenter
who had been saving up,

4
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed that I'm still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
Katsushika, a sigh, a yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,180
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,120
From the pointed hat's water bottle,

9
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:07,460
toward Ōishi Tenmon, the sun sets.

10
00:01:11,620 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow too,
it will end just like this, won't it?

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,060
Katsushika, Kashiwa again,
even happiness is lost.

12
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:31,280
Lewd Photo Panic!

13
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:40,420
Well, if we'd gone there,
we'd have come up empty-handed.

14
00:01:40,420 --> 00:01:42,060
As expected of the chief

15
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:43,940
Not really.

16
00:01:43,940 --> 00:01:44,520
Aaaaah!

17
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:56,440
How's the cake? It's so-so. Do your best not
to let the movie theater day slip away. Thanks.

18
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:03,140
What's this race, I wonder? Oh-ran.

19
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:09,120
Aaaah, yes, I'll go ask right now.
Excuse me.

20
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:19,340
What's this line for? Apparently it's a purikura at Nechoyasu,
and you can make a composite photo with your favorite idol.

21
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:28,440
I'm going to make the Nagano Sector 2 company...
Purikura? What kind of purikura?

22
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:36,200
Yes, it's a purikura! Apparently the latest one lets you take two-shots with five idols,
and it's free.

23
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:39,100
A two-shot with an idol?

24
00:02:40,420 --> 00:02:41,572
That's all it does

25
00:02:41,622 --> 00:02:44,780
So you can take a two-shot
with Suikō Ryōko-chan

26
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:47,220
That's right, Chief.

27
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:48,714
I want one too!

28
00:02:48,764 --> 00:02:52,560
You can even take two-shots
with Aurora Teruyo-sama.

29
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:57,420
Reiko, Chief, shall we go for it?

30
00:02:57,480 --> 00:02:58,260
Shall we do it?

31
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:14,220
There's kind of a naughty thrill to it,
you know.

32
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:14,780
There really is.

33
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:25,720
Come on, it's the super-cheap purikura!

34
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:29,460
And it's the latest model, where you can
take a two-shot with your favorite idol!

35
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:30,360
Welcome!

36
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:32,680
Now that's something to look up to,
a roofer's loincloth!

37
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:34,160
Hey, young ladies, salty and sweet!

38
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:35,960
It's dark in color,
and I want to sink my teeth into it,

39
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:37,860
but with my dentures, I can't get a bite in.

40
00:03:37,860 --> 00:03:39,960
You have to peel it off before you can stick it on,
the printer sticker!

41
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,880
I wonder how this thing works.

42
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:49,760
Well, I've never done it before, you see.

43
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:51,460
It's easy.

44
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:54,180
Stand in front of the machine
and pick the frame you like.

45
00:03:55,720 --> 00:04:01,900
My name is Reiko Akimoto,
and I'm on a budget here, so you stay there.

46
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:14,360
Reiko: Chief, what do you think you're doing, slacking off like this?
Are you really allowed to do purikura during work hours?

47
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:19,360
Well, that's

48
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:24,380
We're just trying to understand
what youth culture is all about,

49
00:04:24,380 --> 00:04:26,380
so we thought we'd
experience it for ourselves.

50
00:04:26,380 --> 00:04:27,340
Exactly.

51
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:33,600
And what were you doing, then?

52
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:37,120
That's what citizen service is, you know.

53
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:39,500
Chief, you say it all the time, don't you?

54
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:41,500
"Work for the citizens."

55
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,660
Citizen service.

56
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:46,300
Then make it free!

57
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:51,237
Anyway,
you said we could get two-shots with idols,

58
00:04:51,287 --> 00:04:54,340
you did get permission
from their agencies, right?

59
00:04:54,420 --> 00:04:56,460
Well, that's not yet.

60
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:59,992
Idiot! That's illegal!

61
00:05:00,042 --> 00:05:03,920
If you take those pictures,
I'll arrest you, got it?

62
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:08,520
Attention, everyone!
From now on, these purikura are free!

63
00:05:08,960 --> 00:05:12,020
Those who paid before
will get their money back!

64
00:05:14,060 --> 00:05:16,400
Now it's my turn, my turn.

65
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:19,240
I'm Tontagomesu,
chief of Katsushika Police Station.

66
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:20,980
Don't forget Tontagomesu.

67
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:24,980
Ohara from the Kameari Park police box,
Chief Ohara.

68
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:31,320
Hey, you bastard,
why are you two getting all the praise?

69
00:05:31,320 --> 00:05:32,620
It's my machine, damn it!

70
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:36,060
That purikura machine has
sucked up my entire fortune!

71
00:05:36,060 --> 00:05:39,940
And you two act like it's nothing that you're taking purikura on duty,
damn you!

72
00:05:44,140 --> 00:05:44,840
Revenge!

73
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:46,920
Even if you're a chief or a station head.

74
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:49,240
I won't let this grudge go unavenged!

75
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:55,600
And so that's how it went.

76
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:58,820
Well, I felt like I'd
gotten ten years younger.

77
00:05:59,820 --> 00:06:02,280
So this is the purikura you took back then?

78
00:06:03,340 --> 00:06:06,260
The Chief and the Station Chief are so cute,
all embarrassed.

79
00:06:06,260 --> 00:06:07,080
I see.

80
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:12,880
Just you wait.

81
00:06:14,020 --> 00:06:18,320
I'll turn their embarrassing photos into
purikura and plaster them all over the place!

82
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:21,860
Right? Right?
I was amazed by that popularity too.

83
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:26,500
Well, I'm heading back to the station.

84
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:28,100
Yes, sir. Understood.

85
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:31,520
Alright.

86
00:06:51,980 --> 00:06:54,420
I'll get in front of them
and catch those dumb faces.

87
00:06:58,720 --> 00:07:00,380
Get ahead, get ahead.

88
00:07:10,020 --> 00:07:12,780
It's just down the second road on the right.

89
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:14,740
Thank you very much.

90
00:07:15,300 --> 00:07:16,080
Well then,

91
00:07:24,460 --> 00:07:25,660
this time for sure,

92
00:07:29,980 --> 00:07:31,100
our chance!

93
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:33,560
Is it full up?

94
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:34,680
Here, let me give you a hand.

95
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:35,660
Excuse me.

96
00:07:35,660 --> 00:07:37,080
It's nothing, really.

97
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:47,260
Let me explain.

98
00:07:47,260 --> 00:07:50,840
What appears through the wall is the Spy-scope,
you see.

99
00:07:50,840 --> 00:07:54,320
The view outside is reflected in the mirror inside,
so you can see it.

100
00:07:54,880 --> 00:07:59,600
Attach this in front of a digital camera, and
you can snap the Chief's dopey face all you want!

101
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:06,020
This'll be perfect!

102
00:08:07,020 --> 00:08:07,920
What's this guy's deal?

103
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:09,360
Get out of the way, you bastard!

104
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:12,380
Stop it, idiot!

105
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:15,260
Hey! Are you all right?

106
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:17,480
Hey! I'm fine!

107
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:24,400
This time for sure.

108
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:27,080
Excuse me...

109
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:37,040
Y-yes, what is it?

110
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:40,920
There you go!

111
00:08:40,920 --> 00:08:42,760
Whoa!

112
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:44,220
Pardon me!

113
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:46,840
What?

114
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:49,860
Just a plain old exhibitionist

115
00:08:57,080 --> 00:08:59,320
It's still not working,
it's still not working.

116
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:01,900
Is the baby in your belly crying?

117
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:05,200
W-what, what, what?

118
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:05,960
What?

119
00:09:09,060 --> 00:09:12,340
This is OK, right?

120
00:09:12,900 --> 00:09:13,420
Mm.

121
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:14,840
Mm.

122
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:15,140
Mm.

123
00:09:16,920 --> 00:09:17,440
Mm.

124
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:25,780
I'll make you realize what
happens when you anger the Chief.

125
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:27,440
Take that!

126
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:27,700
Mm.

127
00:09:34,020 --> 00:09:36,160
Right in the middle of your belly,
you bellybutton!

128
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:45,380
Who said such a thing?

129
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:50,480
Chief, what is this?

130
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:53,380
I don't know, I don't know, Jimmy!

131
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:13,480
That gave me a little shiver.

132
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:29,600
Who on earth would do such a thing?

133
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:33,980
I see. So you're saying you don't
remember taking these pictures?

134
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:38,380
Of course not! I've never once
been seen looking like such a mess!

135
00:10:38,980 --> 00:10:40,580
I see, I see. Understood.

136
00:10:40,580 --> 00:10:42,060
What? Is that really true?

137
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:46,160
Look, see the faces in these two photos?

138
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:48,580
No, no, they're exactly the same face!

139
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:50,520
These are composite photos, you know.

140
00:10:51,020 --> 00:10:52,380
Composite photos?

141
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:53,900
Aaaaaah!

142
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:57,780
It's a purikura that makes
composite photos with idols!

143
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:00,820
So it was that guy's doing after all.

144
00:11:01,380 --> 00:11:04,740
Curse you, you'd better be ready, Ryotsu!

145
00:11:08,380 --> 00:11:11,760
I wonder what their faces look like right now.
Serves them right!

146
00:11:11,760 --> 00:11:14,300
Now, where should I put up the rest?

147
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:36,740
I've been had! You put my face
on wanted posters all over town!

148
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:39,160
I told you! I told you! I told you!

149
00:11:39,160 --> 00:11:39,400
Idiot!

150
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:41,880
Ha-ha!

151
00:11:43,460 --> 00:11:45,320
So this is the culprit

152
00:11:46,340 --> 00:11:47,640
Yes, welcome!

153
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:50,360
Lucky you, you're tough

154
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,300
That's why...

155
00:11:52,300 --> 00:11:52,960
Seriously?

156
00:11:58,620 --> 00:12:01,280
My boyfriend was, like, all over me a bit.

157
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:02,380
Wait, seriously?

158
00:12:02,940 --> 00:12:03,880
Super bad!

159
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:22,020
Would they go this far?!

160
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:44,180
Hey, hey.

161
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:46,280
Did you hear about the
purikura incident the other day?

162
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:47,360
That was the worst, wasn't it?

163
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:49,420
That was the caveman's doing too, right?

164
00:12:49,420 --> 00:12:51,100
Who are you calling a caveman?

165
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:54,820
So you did another survey, didn't you?

166
00:12:54,820 --> 00:12:58,760
A survey of police stations
across Tokyo's 23 wards.

167
00:12:58,760 --> 00:13:00,620
Men who don't want to get married...

168
00:13:00,620 --> 00:13:02,220
Number one, proudly taking the top spot!

169
00:13:02,220 --> 00:13:03,420
Kankichi Ryotsu

170
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:05,960
Once again,
you're way out in front at the top.

171
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:09,200
Yeah. And the gap with the NEET
has widened since last time.

172
00:13:09,700 --> 00:13:12,620
The vulgar sticker incident the other day was the problem,
wasn't it.

173
00:13:13,140 --> 00:13:14,100
That's right.

174
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:15,600
Honda.

175
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:18,740
What, you too?
Do you have a complaint about me?

176
00:13:18,740 --> 00:13:20,940
But look right there.

177
00:13:21,460 --> 00:13:24,400
I'm ranked seventh from the bottom too.

178
00:13:24,400 --> 00:13:25,380
So you are.

179
00:13:26,820 --> 00:13:30,520
So you're unpopular with the parents too,
just like me?

180
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:31,400
Look, Kunyaru.

181
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:35,980
No, it's not like that. I was disliked
just for being close with a senior officer.

182
00:13:36,540 --> 00:13:39,580
Speaking of which, last time you
weren't ranked at all, were you?

183
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:43,740
What are you doing?!

184
00:13:44,620 --> 00:13:46,380
This is nothing! It's a fake!

185
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:48,460
It's not a fake!

186
00:13:49,280 --> 00:13:51,920
You just made this up at random, didn't you!

187
00:13:52,080 --> 00:13:54,080
Unforgivable! What a terrible person!

188
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:57,660
Just you wait!
I'll show you the proof right now!

189
00:13:58,680 --> 00:14:00,520
How long are we supposed to keep waiting?

190
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:04,400
Aaaaaaah

191
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:06,140
Aaaaaaah

192
00:14:06,140 --> 00:14:07,340
Aaaaaaah

193
00:14:07,340 --> 00:14:08,000
Aaaaaaah

194
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:12,180
Well, there are still cases like this,
you know.

195
00:14:13,460 --> 00:14:15,240
Men women don't want to marry

196
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:16,380
Ryotsu Kankichi

197
00:14:16,380 --> 00:14:19,600
Reason: barbaric, vulgar, I hate his face

198
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:21,500
Men women don't want to marry

199
00:14:21,500 --> 00:14:23,180
That's Ryotsu Kankichi.

200
00:14:23,180 --> 00:14:25,420
Reason: he's not even human

201
00:14:25,420 --> 00:14:27,180
He should hurry back to the jungle.

202
00:14:27,180 --> 00:14:29,140
Men women don't want to marry

203
00:14:29,140 --> 00:14:30,520
Of course, Ryotsu Kankichi.

204
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:38,560
I hate breathing the same air, I hate his very existence.
Stop it, I've already told you, shit!

205
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:49,000
Yeah, Ryo-chan is worst again, so we won't get invited today either What?
What's this about? They're holding a moon-viewing party at the women's dormitory.

206
00:14:49,420 --> 00:14:56,900
The Chief and I are invited too, but didn't you know, senior?
I didn't know, damn it. Nobody told me, did they?

207
00:14:56,900 --> 00:14:59,780
Hey, there's apparently a game tournament
as part of the entertainment, too.

208
00:15:00,220 --> 00:15:03,290
If I remember right, first prize
is that PC game you were wanting,

209
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:04,640
"Fight da Pee..."

210
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:06,440
What!? R-really?!

211
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:07,780
Of course it's really true!

212
00:15:08,300 --> 00:15:09,260
It's you two again.

213
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:12,940
Nyah-nyah,
we're not inviting cavemen like you, are we?

214
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:17,540
Anyway, Reiko, do you have any fun ideas?

215
00:15:17,780 --> 00:15:20,340
Honestly,
we still haven't settled on an event idea,

216
00:15:20,460 --> 00:15:22,960
so it's just moon-viewing,
karaoke, and a game tournament.

217
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:27,260
Well, Ryo-chan's good at
this sort of thing, though.

218
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:28,880
Eeeeeeh?

219
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,300
What's with that look?

220
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:33,480
Ryo-chan, got any good ideas?

221
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:35,820
Who would do anything for you lot?

222
00:15:35,820 --> 00:15:39,360
Senpai,
you should butter them up while you can.

223
00:15:39,360 --> 00:15:40,640
And they'll be serving good food too.

224
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:43,760
Speaking of which,
we're broke after the purikura.

225
00:15:43,760 --> 00:15:46,960
It's a chance to stock up on food,
and the game software is tempting too.

226
00:15:47,620 --> 00:15:50,820
How about watching fireflies
along with the moon-viewing?

227
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:52,940
Fireflies?!

228
00:15:53,400 --> 00:15:54,540
At this time of year?

229
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:56,760
I've got an acquaintance who can arrange it.

230
00:15:58,260 --> 00:16:00,180
We can get about fifty of them.

231
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:02,780
That sounds lovely. Let's go with that.

232
00:16:02,780 --> 00:16:05,620
Moon-viewing and fireflies, how romantic.

233
00:16:05,620 --> 00:16:06,260
But

234
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:09,680
If we invite this caveman
in exchange for that,

235
00:16:09,680 --> 00:16:11,280
everyone's going to think we're super poor.

236
00:16:11,280 --> 00:16:13,380
As long as we talk about the fireflies,
we'll be fine.

237
00:16:13,380 --> 00:16:15,140
Besides, Ryo-chan is strong.

238
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:18,740
If we invite him, he'd be a huge help
with setting up the venue, wouldn't he?

239
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:23,540
But if the fireflies fall through,
we'll send him home right away.

240
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:26,120
Leave it to me.

241
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:30,840
Make way, make way!
Coming through, coming through!

242
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:32,600
Here we go, heave-ho!

243
00:16:33,160 --> 00:16:34,780
Make way, make way!

244
00:16:35,640 --> 00:16:39,080
Konto-senpai, you're good at
this kind of thing, aren't you?

245
00:16:42,860 --> 00:16:44,920
That turned out pretty impressive,
didn't it.

246
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:48,300
Alright, then I'll go get the fireflies.

247
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:49,500
Yo-chan!

248
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:53,020
We're all set on our end, look.

249
00:16:53,020 --> 00:16:55,300
It's not really a party anymore.

250
00:16:55,774 --> 00:17:00,040
You're joking! What are you saying?!
We already paid for the fireflies!

251
00:17:00,660 --> 00:17:02,240
Hey! You can't cancel now!

252
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:03,380
What happened?

253
00:17:03,440 --> 00:17:07,000
Komachi and Naoko went out on
patrol and still haven't come back.

254
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,520
No matter how many times we call them on the radio,
they don't respond.

255
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:12,940
Something seems off, so I was
thinking of going to look for them now.

256
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:17,000
Is that so...
Do you think something happened?

257
00:17:17,300 --> 00:17:18,960
Don't you have any idea
what might have happened?

258
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:20,083
Come to think of it,

259
00:17:20,133 --> 00:17:23,560
yesterday we impounded a biker
gang's car for illegal parking.

260
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:27,420
Wasn't it something like the Night Riders?

261
00:17:27,780 --> 00:17:28,820
Night Riders?

262
00:17:29,260 --> 00:17:31,020
They're a notorious bunch of thugs.

263
00:17:31,020 --> 00:17:32,100
Come on, Honda!

264
00:17:32,100 --> 00:17:33,300
Forget it.

265
00:17:33,700 --> 00:17:34,660
Count on you, Honda.

266
00:17:35,320 --> 00:17:36,100
Leave it to me.

267
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:41,360
Are they okay?

268
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:43,880
If the Night Riders are involved...

269
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:46,220
There are over a hundred of them, you know.

270
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:50,100
Honda.

271
00:17:50,100 --> 00:17:52,480
You know where they're
likely to hang out, right?

272
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:53,420
Autom, right?

273
00:17:53,420 --> 00:17:54,300
We can't let them get away.

274
00:18:07,980 --> 00:18:11,580
You've got some nerve nabbing us, you bitch!

275
00:18:17,340 --> 00:18:19,860
Idiot, shut your mouth, you bitch!

276
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:23,700
I'll teach you exactly what
happens when you defy us!

277
00:18:23,960 --> 00:18:27,220
Hey, bring her over here!

278
00:18:27,320 --> 00:18:37,300
Go on! Go on!

279
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:41,020
With this, we'll turn your nudes into
stickers and plaster them all over town!

280
00:18:41,020 --> 00:18:41,780
Nooo!

281
00:18:42,180 --> 00:18:43,340
Hey, we can't back down now!

282
00:18:54,020 --> 00:18:55,120
Who the hell are you?

283
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:04,500
Looks like we made it in time.

284
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:05,460
Angel formation!

285
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:09,260
Aaaaaah!

286
00:19:11,940 --> 00:19:13,620
Is that all your strength amounts to?

287
00:19:16,580 --> 00:19:19,720
Honda! You won't need the dye!
Go all out and tear them apart!

288
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:40,280
Aaaaaah!

289
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:53,480
We've pretty much cleaned up. So what now

290
00:19:53,990 --> 00:19:55,700
Damn it!

291
00:19:57,400 --> 00:20:00,220
This is how it's done! Whoaaaa!

292
00:20:00,220 --> 00:20:00,720
Komachi!

293
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:01,520
You bastard!

294
00:20:04,320 --> 00:20:04,880
Take this!

295
00:20:05,060 --> 00:20:06,640
Shut up! You coward!

296
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:08,780
Yeah, I'm a coward, so what!

297
00:20:08,940 --> 00:20:10,440
Not that I'm one to talk!

298
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:11,660
What are you talking about?!

299
00:20:17,740 --> 00:20:18,800
Don't underestimate us, hey!

300
00:20:19,100 --> 00:20:20,580
Hey, when it counts, I'll step up!

301
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:22,920
Idiot! You walked right
into this place on your own!

302
00:20:23,260 --> 00:20:24,820
There's no way out now, is there!

303
00:20:30,220 --> 00:20:31,240
Stand back, Komachi!

304
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:39,400
Komachi!

305
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:47,440
Attack all at once!

306
00:20:52,900 --> 00:20:55,280
W-wait...

307
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:02,540
Yes!

308
00:21:03,080 --> 00:21:03,820
They're here!

309
00:21:05,540 --> 00:21:07,060
U-um, s-stop it!

310
00:21:08,080 --> 00:21:36,560
Whoaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa...

311
00:21:38,060 --> 00:21:43,700
Right? I've kind of changed my opinion of him.
Now that you mention it, he does have a sort of wild side.

312
00:21:43,700 --> 00:21:50,200
I find him attractive. Yeah, once you're married he's probably surprisingly gentle.
Better than some soft, wimpy guy.

313
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:56,660
Maybe. Looks like Ryo-chan's reputation has really gone up.
Yeah, it has.

314
00:21:57,320 --> 00:22:03,920
Okay, fifty fireflies, that's right, right?
At this time of year, could you sell me some fireflies, please? Give me a discount on those fireflies.

315
00:22:03,920 --> 00:22:12,340
No way, I'm joking! I got them because we need them now.
I'm not giving them to you for free, though. One costs 1,000 or 2,000 yen, you know.

316
00:22:12,920 --> 00:22:18,760
But what should I do?
3,000 yen plus consumption tax.

317
00:22:19,720 --> 00:22:25,420
Sold! Deal! That's a profit of 157,500 yen

318
00:22:25,420 --> 00:22:30,380
That said, how am I going to
cover up the moon-viewing party?

319
00:22:33,140 --> 00:22:34,900
Ryo-chan's really late, isn't he?

320
00:22:35,760 --> 00:22:37,360
No, he's going to be late.

321
00:22:37,360 --> 00:22:39,620
Finally he's here. Hurry up, Ryotsu!

322
00:22:40,100 --> 00:22:43,460
Since we're going to see fireflies,
the Chief has come all the way here himself.

323
00:22:43,460 --> 00:22:44,680
Now, now, Ohara-kun.

324
00:22:44,680 --> 00:22:46,940
Yes, yes, don't rush, don't rush.

325
00:22:56,600 --> 00:22:57,740
It's beautiful.

326
00:22:57,740 --> 00:22:59,220
How romantic.

327
00:22:59,220 --> 00:23:02,920
You know, we've been misunderstanding
"mass production" this whole time.

328
00:23:02,920 --> 00:23:03,760
Sorry.

329
00:23:03,760 --> 00:23:06,280
As long as you understand, that's all.

330
00:23:06,280 --> 00:23:09,800
Hey, this is weird.
These fireflies aren't blinking at all!

331
00:23:09,800 --> 00:23:11,120
Now that you mention it, yeah.

332
00:23:11,120 --> 00:23:11,920
Gulp!

333
00:23:11,920 --> 00:23:15,220
Ken, look, isn't it pretty?

334
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,320
Whoa, a cockroach!

335
00:23:29,120 --> 00:23:30,260
What? Did they figure it out?

336
00:23:30,660 --> 00:23:33,000
The cockroach has been
painted with fluorescent paint!

337
00:23:38,100 --> 00:24:02,500
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu...

338
00:24:05,980 --> 00:24:08,860
Hey, hey, old man,
what a flashy lifestyle you're living!

339
00:24:09,260 --> 00:24:12,500
Eating greasy stuff like that,
and you're already 106, you know!

340
00:24:12,500 --> 00:24:15,120
At least think about your
age and show some restraint.

341
00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:17,440
Don't come crying to me when
the reaper comes for you.

342
00:24:17,920 --> 00:24:21,080
Next time, the Explosive Grandpa Power,
you can count on it!

343
00:24:30,620 --> 00:24:37,300
People gossip that I'm a
woman who can't fall in love,

344
00:24:37,300 --> 00:24:41,940
but I have a mountain
of things I want to do.

345
00:24:41,940 --> 00:24:52,020
I want to ride my motorcycle
across the vast desert.

346
00:24:52,020 --> 00:24:59,180
I want to be freer than a bird.

347
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:07,100
A lady's dreams that change
as fast as a kaleidoscope.

348
00:25:07,100 --> 00:25:07,560
me

349
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:09,960
me

350
00:25:11,100 --> 00:25:12,300
me

351
00:25:19,360 --> 00:25:20,760
me

352
00:25:20,760 --> 00:25:23,120
me

353
00:25:23,120 --> 00:25:25,900
me

354
00:25:25,900 --> 00:25:27,040
me

355
00:25:27,040 --> 00:25:29,440
me

356
00:25:29,440 --> 00:25:29,620
me

357
00:25:33,960 --> 00:25:35,360
me

358
00:25:35,360 --> 00:25:36,400
me

359
00:25:36,400 --> 00:25:36,600
me

360
00:25:36,600 --> 00:25:36,620
me

361
00:25:37,100 --> 00:25:40,920
Thank you for watching.

